=== SITUATIONAL CONTEXT ===
<%= @context_block %>

=== SCENE SUMMARY ===
<%= @scene_summary %>

=== ROLLS TO QUALIFY ===
<%= @rolls_json %>

=== TAKE 10 / TAKE 20 RULES ===
- Take 10: A character can Take 10 on any skill check if NOT under immediate danger or
  distraction. This means no active combat, no imminent threats, no time pressure that
  would prevent careful action. Taking 10 treats the d20 roll as 10.
- Take 20: A character can Take 20 if they can Take 10 AND there are no consequences for
  failure (e.g. setting off a trap, falling, taking damage). Taking 20 requires 20x the
  normal time. Treats the d20 roll as 20.
- Take 10/20 only applies to SKILL CHECKS, never to attack rolls, saving throws, or
  ability checks.

=== SITUATIONAL MODIFIER RULES ===
- Flanking: +2 attack bonus when two allies threaten the same enemy from opposite sides.
- High ground: +1 attack bonus for melee attacks from higher elevation.
- Cover: +4 AC bonus (partial cover +2, improved cover +8).
- Surprise: flat-footed targets lose Dex bonus to AC.
- Circumstance bonuses: any environmental advantage (e.g. braced against a wall, calm
  conditions for concentration, well-lit area for searching).
- Only include modifiers that the current situation actually supports. Do NOT invent
  advantages not present in the context.

=== INSTRUCTIONS ===
For each roll, determine:
- take_10_eligible: true/false based on whether the character is free from danger and distraction.
- take_20_eligible: true/false based on Take 10 eligibility PLUS no failure consequences PLUS time available.
- take_10_value / take_20_value: the character's skill modifier + 10 or + 20. Use the modifier
  from the roll's skill if available, or estimate from the character's abilities.
- situational_modifiers: array of applicable bonuses/penalties from the situation.

Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences):
{
  "qualifications": [
    {
      "skill": "Perception",
      "take_10_eligible": true,
      "take_20_eligible": false,
      "take_10_value": 15,
      "take_20_value": null,
      "situational_modifiers": [
        { "source": "well-lit campfire", "bonus": 2, "type": "circumstance" }
      ],
      "reasoning": "Character is at a safe camp with no threats, but cannot Take 20 because there is implied time pressure from the quest."
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Overall assessment of the character's situational state (1-2 sentences)"
}
